+### Separate iOS shader delivery
+
+- **Symptom:** a shader-heavy IPA is too large or contains too many resources for a player's sideload workflow.
+- **Cause:** both compiled Metal libraries and matching fragment learning sources are inside the signed app bundle. Removing them alone leaves the loader looking in the bundle.
+- **Fix:** an opt-in bundle manifest, `dm/external-shaders.json`, selects `Documents/msl`. The separate ZIP contains `msl/pack.json` with identical manifest bytes and `msl/b-<chain>/` with the original resources. The bundle retains only that chain's small `inputs.tsv`. Before host preload, the shell checks manifest identity, input stamp and directory-entry count; a missing, wrong or incomplete pack shows a Files installation hint and does not start the game. Preparation and runtime loading use the same selected root. These are identity/completeness checks, not a per-member cryptographic integrity scan. Existing bundled builds keep their original path, and saves, RomFS and shader caches are preserved. Native Foundation fixtures exercise the production locator; physical-device installation remains untested.
+- **Found on:** [Super Mario Odyssey](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md), splitting the F5 package after a user-reported sideload failure.
+
+### Precompiled shader preparation inventory
+
+- **Symptom:** Play waits again on every launch even though the selected pack contains compiled Metal libraries.
+- **Cause:** source discovery sorted the NVN directory and opened every `.metallib` header before deciding there were no source-form libraries. Preparation also selected the first external `b-` directory independently of the pack locator.
+- **Fix:** after matching the app-owned schema-1 manifest bytes, bundled input stamp, resource count and declared binary/fragment filename counts, retain the selected directory in process memory. Preparation uses that exact directory and skips NVN listing/header probes only for this compiled-pack contract. Legacy manifests retain content-based discovery. GL/Vulkan preparation and on-demand fragment learning sidecars stay independent. This is an installation identity/inventory contract, not a guarantee against same-count content corruption; Metal validates libraries on actual load. No user environment boolean enables the fast path. Monotonic logs separate pack validation, preparation listing/probes, preload/join and first present submission (which does not classify image content).
+- **Found on:** [Super Mario Odyssey](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md), F6 continuation after the user reported repeatable waits after Play. Device timings and acceptance remain open; the shader chain and external ZIP are unchanged.
+
