+### Vertex fetches past a stream's bound size
+
+- **Symptom:** hard-edged translucent slabs and triangles that move with the camera, including white wedges in Odyssey's Cascade Kingdom waterfall mist.
+- **Cause:** Maxwell fetches zeros past a bound vertex stream. Metal instead reads the following pool bytes. Odyssey's half-resolution composite draws nine vertices from a stream holding only three, so an unintended triangle composites the mist twice.
+- **Fix:** before opening the draw encoder, bound-range arithmetic uses the shader inputs and the last direct vertex or instance. Out-of-range streams use a copy padded with zeros; pulling, transform feedback, single geometry capture and CPU-converted inputs use the same semantics. Ported from upstream commit `1c54ea02264cef4abd66fe5767d68fccdf6bd8ff` (#558). The native arithmetic fixture covers 78 checks; the Metal readback tests are `t_vbuf` and `t_pull`.
+- **Open:** general indexed per-vertex streams, indirect draws and batched geometry captures remain unbounded. Windows native fixtures do not establish GPU or iPad acceptance.
+- **Found on:** [Super Mario Odyssey](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md).
+
+### Replaced textures and argument reuse
+
+- **Symptom:** cached argument blocks keep a replaced texture's resource ID, or a draw attempts to use an encoder ended by a texture upgrade.
+- **Cause:** argument invalidation omitted the serial generation; texture-view upgrades may close the render pass while arguments are bound.
+- **Fix:** argument reuse tracks the texture serial generation. If binding ends the encoder, re-encode once on a new pass; a second closure reports and skips the draw. Sampler creation also honors the game's LOD bias within Metal's supported range. These are bounded host fixes from upstream `971d336516a20dde998f0ede29db7e380a8ee6dd` and `81ccacf2891e2ef7687bb63a48451e704887b3e2`.
+- **Found on:** upstream Need for Speed: Hot Pursuit Remastered (ended encoder); no Odyssey-specific trigger or performance gain has been measured. Native resource-rebind fixtures cover 80 checks; real GPU validation remains separate.
